{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SEAM ANALYSIS + REFERENCE CENSUS (pre-extraction, at origin/main 75cdfec3572; file is 794 LOC — grew 787->794 since ticket filing).\n\nCLUSTER (last-synced peer state, ADR 0026 + ticket 88d9), all in src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py:\n- _BASELINE_FIELDS (L105-112) — read only by BindingStore.set_baseline (L472). No external CODE reader: the mentions in inbound_fields.py:208 and adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:396 are comments/docstrings only, as are the test-file mentions.\n- get_baseline (L443) / set_baseline (L459) / get_peer_parent (L480) / set_peer_parent (L496) / seed_baselines_from_snapshot (L516). Internal call graph: seed_baselines_from_snapshot -> set_baseline; set_baseline -> normalize_baseline_value (inbound_fields) + _BASELINE_FIELDS. All five touch ONLY self._data['bindings'] — no coupling to save()/_load()/retire/get_rotation. Clean seam; no import cycle (inbound_fields imports nothing from the reconciler).\n\nEXTERNAL CONSUMERS (grep census incl. getattr-as-string sites, per AGENTS.md):\n- get_peer_parent: outbound_field_diff.py:199 (getattr), inbound_differ.py:244 (getattr), binding_walk.py (import-level use), tests\n- set_peer_parent: reconcile.py:554 (getattr, _advance_peer_parent)\n- get_baseline: outbound_field_diff.py, inbound_differ.py, classify.py, adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py\n- set_baseline: reconcile.py (_advance_baselines), apply_inbound_records.py:267 (getattr)\n- seed_baselines_from_snapshot: reconcile.py + integration tests\nAll consumers call these as METHODS on the store object (often via getattr(binding_store, 'name')), so keeping thin delegating methods preserves every call site and test double untouched.\n\nLOADER HAZARD CHECKED: test_binding_store.py / test_binding_baseline.py / test_binding_absence_lifecycle.py / test_multipass_stateful.py load binding_store.py via importlib.util.spec_from_file_location. binding_store already does absolute imports (rebar_reconciler.get_rotation, rebar_reconciler.inbound_fields) that resolve under that loader, so an absolute import of the new module resolves identically. monkeypatch sites: test_get_rotation_heldout.py:286 patches binding_store.os.replace, test_reconcile_idempotency.py:311 patches _now_iso — both stay in binding_store; unaffected.\n\nPLAN: new module rebar_reconciler/peer_state.py (>=100 LOC) holding _BASELINE_FIELDS + five free functions taking the bindings dict; BindingStore keeps thin delegates (public surface unchanged). New direct unit tests (no BindingStore) incl. absence-semantics pins: absent baseline -> None (local-wins), absent peer parent -> None (no clear)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785858322764530001,"uuid":"38e36de7-7dd6-4635-81f1-70c3acf4254f"}